[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ngodn/CustomShellSystem/main/CCS/docs/media/v1.0.0-alpha.1/ccs-clip-4.gif[/img][/center]

I built Custom Combat System to let you choose the animation each attack of your weapon plays. Put an enemy's swing on your light chain, a heavy from another weapon on your finisher, a boss move on your charged attack, then save the set as a preset and share the file. For each slot you choose how far it goes: keep your weapon's timing and hit numbers with only the animation changed, or take the move's own timing, its damage multiplier and poise damage, and even its weapon in your hand for the swing. Base damage and Resolve are always your weapon's.

[size=4][i][b][color=#ff7700]This is an alpha and I am releasing it now to gather feedback, ideas and bug reports before the first full version.[/color][/b][/i][/size]

[size=4][b]What you can do[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Thirteen slots: light L1 L2 L3, light finisher LF, charged light LC, the same five for heavy, and the sprint attacks S+L and S+H.[/*]
[*]Candidates for every slot: all player weapons' moves, the enemy attacks that use the player's skeleton (so they play on your body), and any new attack animation the running game lists after a patch.[/*]
[*]Per-slot settings on the right panel: Speed, Feel (the game's timing or the move's own), Damage (the move's hit numbers or your weapon's), and Visual (keep your weapon in hand or show the move's own weapon for the swing).[/*]
[*]Presets: save, load and delete your sets. They are plain JSON files you can share.[/*]
[*]Search and filter the candidate list by typing.[/*]
[*]A master switch that puts every attack back to the weapon's own animation at once.[/*]
[/list]

